				"The storm crackles overhead as Uchiha Sasuke stands poised in the center of a crumbling battlefield, his spiky black hair whipping violently against an unseen gale, eyes glowing crimson-red with chakra-infused fury — a silent vow etched beneath clenched teeth and sweat-streaked cheeks — he grips the hilt of his sword so tightly it trembles at its core, fingers digging deep into leather-wrapped gauntlets as if anchoring himself to something unyielding; suddenly, lightning forks behind him, illuminating every muscle tensed in anticipation, then explodes outward in blinding white-hot flashes that momentarily blind the world before snapping back into shadow, casting jagged silhouettes over shattered stone and twisted metal debris surrounding him, while distant screams echo faintly off collapsing towers, swallowed instantly by thunder’s roar, and yet within this chaos, there remains only his breath — shallow but deliberate — held between rage and resolve — as though preparing to unleash not just blade nor force, but destiny itself upon whatever lies ahead… now, without warning, he lunges forward, body slicing through air like a comet tearing open nightfall, sword arcing upward toward heavens where stars flicker ominously — blades gleam silver under moonlight streaks bleeding down from bruised skies — and silence falls heavier than ever around him, broken only by the whisper of fabric ripping free from armor clashing against earth — yes — here begins the endgame..."
